 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to accept new public water and sanitary sewer mains, fire hydrant assemblies, sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located 3161 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Hamilton Church Townhomes (MWS Project Nos. 25-WL-80 and 25-SL-184 and Proposal No. 2026M-097ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 853 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 2,996 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), two fire hydrant assemblies, 20 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located 3161 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Hamilton Church Townhomes, is needed to construct Project Nos. 25-WL-80 and 25-SL-184; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M097ES-001 on October 8, 2026, for the acceptance of said water and sanitary sewer mains, fire hydrant assemblies, sanitary sewer manholes and easements. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 853 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 2,996 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), two fire hydrant assemblies, 20 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located 3161 Hamilton Church Road, also known as Hamilton Church Townhomes, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference:\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n15000011900\t\t\t\t\t3161 Hamilton Church Road\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n\n"
}
